  "details": "I've been trying to implement some kind of decent moving platform solution, but all methods have drawbacks and the easiest method of teleporting the player per frame looks perfect locally, but networking delays make it hard to make a moving platform look good for everyone on the same platform. If we have some ability to override or set a location of a player in a way that could allow us to offset/fix that position networking delay, like letting us set the priority networking position of a player to some transform maybe, that would make moving platforms extremely easy to make, and open up a lot of possibilities for more dynamic and fluid worlds.",
